; model_growth_onto_the_maximum: the other half of the boundary in
; model_growth_past_the_maximum.
;
; One variable below the maximum, REDUCE's auxiliary variable lands
; exactly on MAX_ALLOCATION_SIZE = 2^32 - 1 = 4294967295 and is admitted.
; The pair is what pins the bound: a single refusing vector would pass
; equally against an implementation that refused every growth.
;
; REDUCE pushes the auxiliary variable's index, so the final stack holds
; 4294967294 -- the size the model had before it grew.

PUSH 4294967294
BQMX r0
PUSH 0
PUSH 1
PUSH 5
REDUCE r0
HALT
